<section class="page-heading">
    <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">A QUICK ORIENTATION</p>
        <h1>A thoughtful review, at your pace.</h1>
        <p>Explore any section. There’s no mandatory sequence or hidden change.</p>
    </div>
</section>

<div class="help-grid">
    <section class="panel help-card">
        <h2>How to explore</h2>
        <ol>
            <li>Choose an illustrative city and inspect its fixture offsets.</li>
            <li>Compare a meeting’s local time with its stored UTC instant.</li>
            <li>Confirm intent, skip, or leave the question open.</li>
            <li>Preview the exact batch and approve a simulation.</li>
        </ol>
        <button class="primary" @onclick="OnExplore">Explore the meetings →</button>
    </section>

    <section class="panel help-card">
        <h2>What is real here?</h2>
        <p>Controls, per-meeting choices, filtering, comparisons, and navigation work. People, AI hypotheses, rules, and outcomes are synthetic.</p>
        <p>Side effects stay in this Interactive Server circuit. Nothing is saved to a database or sent to a calendar or model. A fresh connection resets this demo.</p>
        <button class="secondary" @onclick="OnReset">Reset sample workspace ↻</button>
    </section>

    <section class="panel help-card">
        <h2>Calendar connection status</h2>
        <span class="status-badge amber">Not connected</span>
        <p>The separate command-line runner supports Windows sign-in and bounded Graph read probes. This web workspace does not acquire credentials or change meetings.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/feasibility">View calendar pilot feasibility ↗</a>
    </section>

    <section class="panel help-card">
        <h2>Before a real pilot</h2>
        <p>UTC timestamps alone do not establish intent. Production evaluation needs confirmed source rules, applicable locality, current eligibility, exact approval, and atomic guarded writes.</p>
        <p>This demo does not prove provider support, retry safety, invitation delivery, or transition policy. Samples are organizer-owned single instances with internal attendees.</p>
    </section>
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback OnExplore { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback OnReset { get; set; }
}
